=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
The network is operating correctly. A thorough investigation of all five
devices in the dc_clos_bgp topology found no fault at any layer. Every BGP
session is in the Established state with normal keepalive exchanges and no
error events in the FRR logs. All interfaces are up. Both leaf routers carry
the correct routes: leaf_router_0_0 has 10.0.1.0/24 reachable via
spine_router_0_0 (primary) and spine_router_0_1 (valid backup), and
leaf_router_0_1 mirrors that symmetrically for 10.0.0.0/24. End-to-end ping
from pc_0_0 (10.0.0.2) to pc_0_1 (10.0.1.2) succeeds with 0% packet loss
and TTL=61, confirming a clean three-hop path through
leaf_router_0_0 → spine_router_0_0 → leaf_router_0_1. The infra team's
assertion that "one of the spine boxes died" cannot be corroborated: both
spine_router_0_0 and spine_router_0_1 have all FRR daemons running, correct
BGP tables, and valid forwarding entries. The only architectural observation
is that ECMP multipath is not configured, so all inter-rack traffic is
concentrated on spine_router_0_0 (preferred by standard BGP best-path
